# Unholy Annex cast as its left door, then Ritual Chamber's door unlocked by paying its {3}{B}{B} (CR 709.5e): a special
# action, so no stack and no response, taken only with priority and an empty stack during a main phase of its controller's
# turn. Each refusal is made where every other condition holds, so it cannot pass for another reason: with four mana sources
# it is refused for cost (Bot1's own main phase, Annex alone on the battlefield with its colorless costs paid for); with five
# (the Swamp played on turn 3) it is refused in Bot1's beginning of combat step and on Bot2's turn; and on turn 5, in a main
# phase of Bot1's with five sources, it is taken. Unlocking gives the designation (CR 709.5f), so "when you unlock this
# door" triggers (CR 709.5h): a 6/6 Demon. The Room is then both doors at once: both names, a mana value of 8
# (CR 709.5, 709.4b), and the end step ability of Annex now with a Demon to count: the opponent loses 2 and Bot1 gains 2
# (Annex had cost Bot1 2 life at the end of turns 1 and 3, 20 -> 16, and drawn a card each time).

